&lt;b&gt;who had just decided to leave UCSD too&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:24.825 --> 00:39:27.528
&lt;b&gt;Well, so I felt everything was hopeless&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:27.728 --> 00:39:28.062
&lt;b&gt;which was&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:28.062 --> 00:39:30.664
&lt;b&gt;the place I was going didn't seem highly ranked&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:30.831 --> 00:39:31.966
&lt;b&gt;um, and then&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:31.966 --> 00:39:32.866
&lt;b&gt;faculty were also leaving&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:32.866 --> 00:39:34.034
&lt;b&gt;faculty were also leaving&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:34.201 --> 00:39:35.235
&lt;b&gt;But I thought about it and said&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:35.235 --> 00:39:36.870
&lt;b&gt;none of this matters&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:36.971 --> 00:39:37.738
&lt;b&gt;none of it is important&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:37.738 --> 00:39:40.874
&lt;b&gt;what matters is who I'm working with and on what&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:40.874 --> 00:39:42.643
&lt;b&gt;and whether this is something I want to do&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:43.177 --> 00:39:45.479
&lt;b&gt;I think putting aside all this noise&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:45.479 --> 00:39:48.248
&lt;b&gt;this is the only thing I want to care about&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:48.582 --> 00:39:50.050
&lt;b&gt;Mm, that's very interesting&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:50.050 --> 00:39:50.651
&lt;b&gt;Mm&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:50.651 --> 00:39:51.985
&lt;b&gt;So this kind of thing happened several times&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:51.985 --> 00:39:52.519
&lt;b&gt;I just said&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:52.519 --> 00:39:54.755
&lt;b&gt;At SJTU it was also an upward trajectory&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:54.855 --> 00:39:56.957
&lt;b&gt;And then going to&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:56.957 --> 00:39:58.392
&lt;b&gt;UCSD&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:58.392 --> 00:39:59.126
&lt;b&gt;That was also part of it&lt;/b&gt;

00:39:59.126 --> 00:40:00.260
&lt;b&gt;which was&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:00.260 --> 00:40:02.129
&lt;b&gt;Of course&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;b&gt;I'm not saying this has anything to do with me&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:02.129 --> 00:40:04.064
&lt;b&gt;I don't think it has anything to do with me&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:04.064 --> 00:40:06.934
&lt;b&gt;But somehow I feel I can see a place&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:06.934 --> 00:40:08.235
&lt;b&gt;or even a person&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:08.235 --> 00:40:10.337
&lt;b&gt;their upside potential&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:10.337 --> 00:40:11.472
&lt;b&gt;that is, their potential&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:11.605 --> 00:40:12.206
&lt;b&gt;Mm&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:12.206 --> 00:40:14.375
&lt;b&gt;And I'm willing to grow together with those places&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:14.608 --> 00:40:17.611
&lt;b&gt;I think&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;b&gt;This is something I feel quite deeply&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:17.644 --> 00:40:20.647
&lt;b&gt;How long did it take you to find out Professor Tu was going to UCSD?&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:21.148 --> 00:40:23.217
&lt;b&gt;Um, maybe a few months later&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:23.250 --> 00:40:25.052
&lt;b&gt;Right, maybe one or two months later&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:25.119 --> 00:40:26.920
&lt;b&gt;Were you worried at the time?&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:27.020 --> 00:40:28.122
&lt;b&gt;Of course I was worried&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:29.056 --> 00:40:29.556
&lt;b&gt;Right&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:29.556 --> 00:40:33.227
&lt;b&gt;Because Professor Tu is actually very humble&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:33.527 --> 00:40:36.530
&lt;b&gt;extremely capable but very humble&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:36.830 --> 00:40:39.566
&lt;b&gt;So he would always give me a heads-up saying&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:39.566 --> 00:40:40.434
&lt;b&gt;the school I'm going to&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:40.434 --> 00:40:42.202
&lt;b&gt;might be ranked lower&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:42.202 --> 00:40:43.170
&lt;b&gt;you should think about it&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:43.837 --> 00:40:45.239
&lt;b&gt;Right, what did you say?&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:45.672 --> 00:40:47.641
&lt;b&gt;I don't remember very well what I said&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:47.641 --> 00:40:48.876
&lt;b&gt;But again, for me&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:48.876 --> 00:40:50.244
&lt;b&gt;this might not be that important&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:50.544 --> 00:40:51.545
&lt;b&gt;And&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:51.612 --> 00:40:54.181
&lt;b&gt;and at that time it wasn't yet time to make a decision&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:54.181 --> 00:40:55.983
&lt;b&gt;Right, why should I&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:55.983 --> 00:40:58.419
&lt;b&gt;worry in advance about things that haven't happened&lt;/b&gt;

00:40:58.419 --> 00:40:59.820
&lt;b&gt;So I didn't think too much about it&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:00.921 --> 00:41:02.589
&lt;b&gt;Did anyone else make this choice?&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:02.589 --> 00:41:04.224
&lt;b&gt;Among the students Professor Tu communicated with&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:04.525 --> 00:41:06.427
&lt;b&gt;Um, basically none&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:06.427 --> 00:41:08.762
&lt;b&gt;I was the first student he recruited at UCSD&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:09.129 --> 00:41:10.397
&lt;b&gt;I think just based on that&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:10.397 --> 00:41:11.932
&lt;b&gt;Professor Tu must like you very much&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:12.433 --> 00:41:14.668
&lt;b&gt;Um, I think all of this is&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:14.668 --> 00:41:16.336
&lt;b&gt;I think it was also him saving me&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:16.336 --> 00:41:17.204
&lt;b&gt;Um, indeed&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:17.204 --> 00:41:18.772
&lt;b&gt;But this was not only rescuing me at the beginning&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:18.772 --> 00:41:20.674
&lt;b&gt;and then later doing research&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:20.674 --> 00:41:21.775
&lt;b&gt;during the PhD process&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:21.775 --> 00:41:25.045
&lt;b&gt;I think he truly helped me&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:25.045 --> 00:41:28.515
&lt;b&gt;Right, like my internship in Singapore and such&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:28.515 --> 00:41:30.250
&lt;b&gt;you could say we were doing some research&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:30.517 --> 00:41:32.119
&lt;b&gt;but in reality&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:32.119 --> 00:41:33.554
&lt;b&gt;it was still small-scale stuff&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:33.554 --> 00:41:37.558
&lt;b&gt;having someone next to you teaching you&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:37.558 --> 00:41:39.026
&lt;b&gt;the feeling is still different&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:39.393 --> 00:41:42.629
&lt;b&gt;Professor Tu is the type who sits beside your monitor&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:42.830 --> 00:41:44.665
&lt;b&gt;and goes through the code with you line by line&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:44.665 --> 00:41:45.799
&lt;b&gt;that kind of teacher&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:45.799 --> 00:41:48.769
&lt;b&gt;Mm, and he often&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:48.769 --> 00:41:50.737
&lt;b&gt;I think proudly would tell us these things&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:50.737 --> 00:41:52.806
&lt;b&gt;And I think he is very deserving&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:52.806 --> 00:41:54.074
&lt;b&gt;of this pride, meaning&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:54.074 --> 00:41:56.076
&lt;b&gt;he published several papers&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:56.210 --> 00:41:57.377
&lt;b&gt;that actually had an important influence&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:57.377 --> 00:41:59.246
&lt;b&gt;on later computer vision&lt;/b&gt;

00:41:59.246 --> 00:42:02.983
&lt;b&gt;all completed as sole author works&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:03.250 --> 00:42:06.954
&lt;b&gt;And these works didn't have, like now&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:06.954 --> 00:42:07.921
&lt;b&gt;everyone using PyTorch&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:07.921 --> 00:42:10.023
&lt;b&gt;with so many open-source communities&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:10.057 --> 00:42:11.992
&lt;b&gt;so many libraries you can use&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:12.192 --> 00:42:14.194
&lt;b&gt;right, having GPUs&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:14.194 --> 00:42:15.629
&lt;b&gt;in his time there was nothing&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:15.963 --> 00:42:18.132
&lt;b&gt;he had to write from the ground up&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:18.132 --> 00:42:21.168
&lt;b&gt;For example, for a task like image segmentation&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:21.401 --> 00:42:23.036
&lt;b&gt;he had to write from scratch&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:23.203 --> 00:42:24.771
&lt;b&gt;about 50,000 lines of code&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:24.771 --> 00:42:27.074
&lt;b&gt;He even sent me this code to look at&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:27.074 --> 00:42:29.243
&lt;b&gt;That included the lowest level&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:29.243 --> 00:42:31.778
&lt;b&gt;including some distributed training&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:31.778 --> 00:42:33.447
&lt;b&gt;a whole series of things&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:33.447 --> 00:42:34.815
&lt;b&gt;all written in C++&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:35.549 --> 00:42:36.650
&lt;b&gt;Right, 50,000 lines of code&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:37.150 --> 00:42:39.319
&lt;b&gt;I think&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:39.319 --> 00:42:41.955
&lt;b&gt;On one hand I feel I'm very lucky&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:41.955 --> 00:42:42.856
&lt;b&gt;not needing to go through all that&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:42.856 --> 00:42:43.390
&lt;b&gt;But on the other hand&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:43.390 --> 00:42:44.992
&lt;b&gt;I think actually&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:44.992 --> 00:42:49.196
&lt;b&gt;their generation in America&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:49.196 --> 00:42:50.631
&lt;b&gt;these scientists&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:50.631 --> 00:42:52.966
&lt;b&gt;these professors are truly admirable&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:53.433 --> 00:42:55.168
&lt;b&gt;Right, if not for them&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:55.168 --> 00:42:56.203
&lt;b&gt;there would be no us today&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:56.203 --> 00:42:58.539
&lt;b&gt;They actually, um&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:58.539 --> 00:42:59.840
&lt;b&gt;blazed a trail&lt;/b&gt;

00:42:59.840 --> 00:43:01.575
&lt;b&gt;Right, this path didn't originally exist&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:01.608 --> 00:43:02.943
&lt;b&gt;As I said, right&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:02.943 --> 00:43:04.945
&lt;b&gt;publishing a CVPR paper&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:04.945 --> 00:43:07.948
&lt;b&gt;was actually a very, very difficult thing&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:07.948 --> 00:43:10.384
&lt;b&gt;And there was a certain circle&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:10.384 --> 00:43:11.718
&lt;b&gt;a certain fixed circle&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:12.019 --> 00:43:16.056
&lt;b&gt;Right, and I think it required Professor Tu&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:16.056 --> 00:43:18.959
&lt;b&gt;and actually his boss&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:18.959 --> 00:43:20.794
&lt;b&gt;Professor Zhu Songchun&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:20.827 --> 00:43:22.462
&lt;b&gt;and including later people like Fei-Fei (Li Fei-Fei, Stanford professor, co-founder and CEO of World Labs)&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:22.462 --> 00:43:23.197
&lt;b&gt;and so on&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:23.197 --> 00:43:24.198
&lt;b&gt;Professor Fei-Fei&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:24.198 --> 00:43:26.833
&lt;b&gt;everyone blazing this trail&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:27.034 --> 00:43:28.535
&lt;b&gt;so that we have a path to walk&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:28.835 --> 00:43:32.372
&lt;b&gt;Mm, I saw a Xiaohongshu comment saying&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:32.372 --> 00:43:34.675
&lt;b&gt;Xie Saining was unremarkable in China&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:34.942 --> 00:43:36.210
&lt;b&gt;nothing special&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:36.243 --> 00:43:37.844
&lt;b&gt;made a big splash when he got to America&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:37.844 --> 00:43:39.513
&lt;b&gt;So what exactly is the variable?&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:40.747 --> 00:43:43.817
&lt;b&gt;First, I don't think I was unremarkable in China&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:43.817 --> 00:43:45.252
&lt;b&gt;Mm, I don't accept that&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:45.452 --> 00:43:47.054
&lt;b&gt;And I didn't make a big splash in America either&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:47.054 --> 00:43:48.121
&lt;b&gt;I don't accept that either&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:48.388 --> 00:43:51.391
&lt;b&gt;I feel like the things I've done&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:51.592 --> 00:43:54.394
&lt;b&gt;have been a fairly smooth&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:54.394 --> 00:43:56.063
&lt;b&gt;a very gradual process&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:56.363 --> 00:43:59.266
&lt;b&gt;Right, and or rather I think this is also what I hope&lt;/b&gt;

00:43:59.600 --> 00:44:02.235
&lt;b&gt;um, as a researcher, right&lt;/b&gt;

00:44:02.235 --> 00:44:04.972
&lt;b&gt;this kind of science practitioner&lt;/b&gt;

00:44:05.205 --> 00:44:09.042
&lt;b&gt;I hope to be in&lt;/b&gt;

00:44:09.443 --> 00:44:12.913
&lt;b&gt;meaning this is not a momentary&lt;/b&gt;

00:44:13.547 --> 00:44:15.816
&lt;b&gt;burst of hormones or adrenaline&lt;/b&gt;

00:44:16.049 --> 00:44:16.583
&lt;b&gt;this thing&lt;/b&gt;

00:44:16.583 --> 00:44:19.386
&lt;b&gt;might be a lifetime of building&lt;/b&gt;

00:44:20.220 --> 00:44:22.990
&lt;b&gt;a very quiet process&lt;/b&gt;

00:44:22.990 --> 00:44:23.790
&lt;b&gt;I hope&lt;/b&gt;

00:44:23.790 --> 00:44:25.259
&lt;b&gt;to be in such a state&lt;/b&gt;

00:44:25.259 --> 00:44:25.993
&lt;b&gt;When I say such a state&lt;/b&gt;

00:44:25.993 --> 00:44:27.261
&lt;b&gt;it's because I know&lt;/b&gt;

00:44:27.327 --> 00:44:29.196
&lt;b&gt;many people are in this state&lt;/b&gt;

00:44:29.229 --> 00:44:32.399
&lt;b&gt;the researchers I most admire&lt;/b&gt;

00:44:32.399 --> 00:44:33.600
&lt;b&gt;they are in this state&lt;/b&gt;

