&lt;b&gt;because a film also needs to discover a theme&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:28.634 --> 02:52:29.802
&lt;b&gt;it also involves exploration&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:29.802 --> 02:52:32.371
&lt;b&gt;I have a story I want to tell&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:32.471 --> 02:52:34.573
&lt;b&gt;and it shouldn't be that I just stand at this moment&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:34.573 --> 02:52:35.274
&lt;b&gt;and think oh&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:35.274 --> 02:52:36.609
&lt;b&gt;this is how my story goes&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:36.609 --> 02:52:38.878
&lt;b&gt;and then I just go straight toward the finish&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:39.045 --> 02:52:40.179
&lt;b&gt;it shouldn't work that way either&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:40.179 --> 02:52:41.247
&lt;b&gt;you should also go make the film&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:41.247 --> 02:52:42.682
&lt;b&gt;I think you'd have great intuition&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:42.815 --> 02:52:43.950
&lt;b&gt;right&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:43.983 --> 02:52:45.017
&lt;b&gt;yes, exactly right&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:45.017 --> 02:52:47.420
&lt;b&gt;the worst films are the ones that just go through the motions&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:47.420 --> 02:52:47.987
&lt;b&gt;I start with A&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:47.987 --> 02:52:49.488
&lt;b&gt;no conflict along the way&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:49.488 --> 02:52:50.056
&lt;b&gt;and arrive at B&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:50.056 --> 02:52:51.157
&lt;b&gt;and then it's over&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:51.190 --> 02:52:52.158
&lt;b&gt;I just&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:52.158 --> 02:52:53.960
&lt;b&gt;play it for you&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:53.960 --> 02:52:55.661
&lt;b&gt;a good film actually is&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:56.295 --> 02:52:57.763
&lt;b&gt;or, why do we say when writing a paper&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:57.763 --> 02:52:58.864
&lt;b&gt;people say&lt;/b&gt;

02:52:58.864 --> 02:53:00.800
&lt;b&gt;they told the story really well&lt;/b&gt;

02:53:00.800 --> 02:53:03.002
&lt;b&gt;even though this might even have a bit of a narrative&lt;/b&gt;

02:53:03.803 --> 02:53:04.603
&lt;b&gt;storytelling quality&lt;/b&gt;

02:53:04.603 --> 02:53:05.237
&lt;b&gt;mm&lt;/b&gt;

02:53:05.237 --> 02:53:06.972
&lt;b&gt;film is a storytelling process&lt;/b&gt;

02:53:07.740 --> 02:53:08.674
&lt;b&gt;there's a book&lt;/b&gt;

02:53:08.674 --> 02:53:10.609
&lt;b&gt;I actually recommended it to students before&lt;/b&gt;

02:53:10.609 --> 02:53:11.544
&lt;b&gt;I learned from Kaiming&lt;/b&gt;

02:53:11.544 --> 02:53:13.813
&lt;b&gt;I share with people&lt;/b&gt;

02:53:13.813 --> 02:53:15.081
&lt;b&gt;some unexpected books&lt;/b&gt;

02:53:15.081 --> 02:53:16.048
&lt;b&gt;let me recommend a book&lt;/b&gt;

02:53:16.048 --> 02:53:17.650
&lt;b&gt;it's called Story, by Robert McKee&lt;/b&gt;

02:53:17.650 --> 02:53:19.251
&lt;b&gt;mm&lt;/b&gt;

02:53:19.251 --> 02:53:20.086
&lt;b&gt;this book is a book about screenwriting&lt;/b&gt;

02:53:20.086 --> 02:53:21.854
&lt;b&gt;mm&lt;/b&gt;

02:53:21.854 --> 02:53:22.355
&lt;b&gt;but I think this book&lt;/b&gt;

