&lt;b&gt;I've been doing architecture work for so long&lt;/b&gt;

03:05:48.533 --> 03:05:50.535
&lt;b&gt;I think this is the future of Diffusion architectures&lt;/b&gt;

03:05:50.769 --> 03:05:52.537
&lt;b&gt;right, it's not the Diffusion Model&lt;/b&gt;

03:05:52.537 --> 03:05:54.873
&lt;b&gt;what I said, the overall data architecture&lt;/b&gt;

03:05:55.040 --> 03:05:56.608
&lt;b&gt;and the objective&lt;/b&gt;

03:05:56.608 --> 03:05:57.576
&lt;b&gt;are all very important&lt;/b&gt;

03:05:57.809 --> 03:05:59.077
&lt;b&gt;right, but on the architecture side&lt;/b&gt;

03:05:59.077 --> 03:06:02.280
&lt;b&gt;this is an indispensable piece&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:02.280 --> 03:06:02.948
&lt;b&gt;so this is why&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:02.948 --> 03:06:04.850
&lt;b&gt;in the last month we pushed in this direction&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:05.016 --> 03:06:06.218
&lt;b&gt;and the results were very good in the end&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:06.218 --> 03:06:07.953
&lt;b&gt;and we were able to show&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:07.953 --> 03:06:08.820
&lt;b&gt;this really great&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:08.820 --> 03:06:09.855
&lt;b&gt;scaling behavior&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:09.855 --> 03:06:12.090
&lt;b&gt;and we submitted the paper to CVPR&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:12.090 --> 03:06:13.592
&lt;b&gt;and we were all very happy&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:13.592 --> 03:06:14.493
&lt;b&gt;and then the paper got rejected&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:14.493 --> 03:06:15.460
&lt;b&gt;mm&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:15.827 --> 03:06:17.796
&lt;b&gt;right, LeCun apparently tweeted about this&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:17.796 --> 03:06:18.463
&lt;b&gt;yes&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:18.463 --> 03:06:20.465
&lt;b&gt;saying not enough novelty&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:20.465 --> 03:06:22.200
&lt;b&gt;you might have done this thing&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:22.534 --> 03:06:23.535
&lt;b&gt;uh, right&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:23.535 --> 03:06:25.203
&lt;b&gt;you don't have long stretches of math&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:25.203 --> 03:06:27.272
&lt;b&gt;you don't have a long complex structure&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:27.272 --> 03:06:29.374
&lt;b&gt;you came up with a very simple structure&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:29.407 --> 03:06:31.042
&lt;b&gt;and even though you got good results&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:31.042 --> 03:06:33.011
&lt;b&gt;the reviewers weren't convinced&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:33.078 --> 03:06:34.746
&lt;b&gt;mm, right&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:34.746 --> 03:06:35.847
&lt;b&gt;this is another lesson&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:35.847 --> 03:06:36.982
&lt;b&gt;but by that point&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:36.982 --> 03:06:38.850
&lt;b&gt;I had actually started to come around&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:38.850 --> 03:06:40.352
&lt;b&gt;I realized&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:40.352 --> 03:06:43.588
&lt;b&gt;this whole thing about research papers&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:43.688 --> 03:06:46.258
&lt;b&gt;in this huge random process&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:46.758 --> 03:06:47.425
&lt;b&gt;whether you get accepted or not&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:47.425 --> 03:06:49.795
&lt;b&gt;doesn't matter at all&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:49.795 --> 03:06:51.363
&lt;b&gt;so we then submitted to another conference&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:51.363 --> 03:06:52.230
&lt;b&gt;didn't change a thing&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:52.230 --> 03:06:53.832
&lt;b&gt;and it got accepted as an Oral Paper&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:53.832 --> 03:06:55.467
&lt;b&gt;mm, which proves once again&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:55.467 --> 03:06:57.636
&lt;b&gt;this is a completely random process&lt;/b&gt;

03:06:57.869 --> 03:07:00.138
&lt;b&gt;but what happened afterward was more interesting&lt;/b&gt;

03:07:00.138 --> 03:07:01.139
&lt;b&gt;after getting this paper&lt;/b&gt;

03:07:01.139 --> 03:07:02.474
&lt;b&gt;I realized&lt;/b&gt;

03:07:02.474 --> 03:07:04.009
&lt;b&gt;in every dimension&lt;/b&gt;

03:07:04.009 --> 03:07:06.144
&lt;b&gt;this was better than a U-Net based system&lt;/b&gt;

03:07:07.279 --> 03:07:09.347
&lt;b&gt;why not just use this&lt;/b&gt;

03:07:09.381 --> 03:07:12.450
&lt;b&gt;right, you've unified the underlying logic&lt;/b&gt;

03:07:12.450 --> 03:07:14.586
&lt;b&gt;at least on the architecture side, unified the logic&lt;/b&gt;

03:07:14.586 --> 03:07:16.555
&lt;b&gt;you can share a lot of infrastructure&lt;/b&gt;

03:07:16.621 --> 03:07:17.956
&lt;b&gt;it's so efficient&lt;/b&gt;

03:07:17.956 --> 03:07:19.257
&lt;b&gt;results are good and scalable&lt;/b&gt;

03:07:19.257 --> 03:07:20.492
&lt;b&gt;you can build even larger models&lt;/b&gt;

03:07:21.226 --> 03:07:22.394
&lt;b&gt;so we thought&lt;/b&gt;

03:07:22.394 --> 03:07:22.861
&lt;b&gt;this thing&lt;/b&gt;

03:07:22.861 --> 03:07:25.430
&lt;b&gt;once this paper is out, there will definitely be a lot of attention&lt;/b&gt;

03:07:25.630 --> 03:07:26.298
&lt;b&gt;which, by the way&lt;/b&gt;

03:07:26.298 --> 03:07:27.332
&lt;b&gt;there was indeed a lot of attention&lt;/b&gt;

03:07:27.332 --> 03:07:28.834
&lt;b&gt;lots of people discussing it on Twitter&lt;/b&gt;

03:07:29.467 --> 03:07:30.602
&lt;b&gt;but we found, hey&lt;/b&gt;

03:07:30.602 --> 03:07:32.671
&lt;b&gt;nobody was actually using it for anything&lt;/b&gt;

03:07:32.737 --> 03:07:33.772
&lt;b&gt;oh&lt;/b&gt;

