&lt;b&gt;it can't perceive the world at all&lt;/b&gt;

03:30:54.838 --> 03:30:56.607
&lt;b&gt;all this visual knowledge&lt;/b&gt;

03:30:56.807 --> 03:30:57.975
&lt;b&gt;it can't see images&lt;/b&gt;

03:30:57.975 --> 03:30:59.076
&lt;b&gt;it can't see videos either&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:00.010 --> 03:31:00.811
&lt;b&gt;right&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:00.978 --> 03:31:04.047
&lt;b&gt;but it can, through language&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:04.381 --> 03:31:07.217
&lt;b&gt;like Plato's Cave allegory&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:07.651 --> 03:31:10.187
&lt;b&gt;indirectly understand the world&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:10.454 --> 03:31:11.088
&lt;b&gt;that's fine&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:11.088 --> 03:31:12.022
&lt;b&gt;we call it L0&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:12.990 --> 03:31:15.626
&lt;b&gt;L1 is the current multimodal system&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:15.993 --> 03:31:17.761
&lt;b&gt;with slightly better capabilities&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:18.095 --> 03:31:19.496
&lt;b&gt;it's capable of what you'd call show and tell&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:19.496 --> 03:31:21.164
&lt;b&gt;meaning you show it something&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:21.431 --> 03:31:23.433
&lt;b&gt;and then it can tell you&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:23.600 --> 03:31:26.436
&lt;b&gt;some answers about what you showed it&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:26.770 --> 03:31:27.771
&lt;b&gt;right, you ask it a question&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:27.771 --> 03:31:29.873
&lt;b&gt;and it gives you an answer&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:29.873 --> 03:31:30.974
&lt;b&gt;this might be L1&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:31.241 --> 03:31:33.343
&lt;b&gt;then L2, I think, is&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:33.343 --> 03:31:35.779
&lt;b&gt;what I call streaming event cognition&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:35.946 --> 03:31:37.447
&lt;b&gt;meaning now this thing&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:37.447 --> 03:31:40.450
&lt;b&gt;doesn't just look at a static image&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:40.584 --> 03:31:43.954
&lt;b&gt;you'd have a continuous, streamable&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:43.954 --> 03:31:45.055
&lt;b&gt;visual stream like this&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:45.055 --> 03:31:46.189
&lt;b&gt;a visual stream&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:46.823 --> 03:31:47.758
&lt;b&gt;your intelligent system&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:47.758 --> 03:31:49.393
&lt;b&gt;needs to be able to understand this visual stream&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:49.693 --> 03:31:52.429
&lt;b&gt;and be able to process this visual stream&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:52.429 --> 03:31:54.998
&lt;b&gt;and also be able to answer questions&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:54.998 --> 03:31:56.566
&lt;b&gt;be able to understand&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:56.566 --> 03:31:57.734
&lt;b&gt;what's happened&lt;/b&gt;

03:31:58.135 --> 03:32:00.370
&lt;b&gt;right, and then the next stage&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:00.370 --> 03:32:02.406
&lt;b&gt;uh, I call it spatial cognition&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:02.472 --> 03:32:03.340
&lt;b&gt;meaning this is about&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:03.340 --> 03:32:04.174
&lt;b&gt;what I was just saying&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:04.241 --> 03:32:05.142
&lt;b&gt;which is that you&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:05.142 --> 03:32:07.277
&lt;b&gt;at every point in this temporal sequence&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:07.444 --> 03:32:10.847
&lt;b&gt;how to see beyond the present moment&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:10.847 --> 03:32:12.783
&lt;b&gt;to what's really behind it — these&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:12.783 --> 03:32:14.618
&lt;b&gt;the space behind these pixels&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:14.785 --> 03:32:15.218
&lt;b&gt;right&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:15.218 --> 03:32:17.854
&lt;b&gt;this is also something very, very deep for humans&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:17.854 --> 03:32:19.156
&lt;b&gt;a very unique ability&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:20.490 --> 03:32:22.092
&lt;b&gt;and ultimately&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:22.092 --> 03:32:23.427
&lt;b&gt;actually, um&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:23.427 --> 03:32:24.594
&lt;b&gt;I think the endgame is&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:24.594 --> 03:32:26.630
&lt;b&gt;we need a predictive world model&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:26.697 --> 03:32:29.533
&lt;b&gt;yes, some kind of predictive world model&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:30.133 --> 03:32:32.436
&lt;b&gt;this is what can tell you&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:32.569 --> 03:32:35.472
&lt;b&gt;everything about the real world you observe&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:35.972 --> 03:32:37.607
&lt;b&gt;yes, I think&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:37.607 --> 03:32:40.077
&lt;b&gt;what I want to convey through this paper is&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:40.077 --> 03:32:42.813
&lt;b&gt;we're building a staircase&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:42.946 --> 03:32:44.281
&lt;b&gt;step by step&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:44.281 --> 03:32:47.017
&lt;b&gt;leading toward a future with a world model&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:47.017 --> 03:32:47.851
&lt;b&gt;mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:47.851 --> 03:32:49.553
&lt;b&gt;um, although we may not know&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:49.553 --> 03:32:52.055
&lt;b&gt;exactly how to define this world model&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:52.055 --> 03:32:53.023
&lt;b&gt;at least in this paper&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:53.023 --> 03:32:55.392
&lt;b&gt;we won't attempt to do that definitional work&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:55.659 --> 03:32:58.862
&lt;b&gt;but we can identify&lt;/b&gt;

03:32:58.862 --> 03:33:02.132
&lt;b&gt;which capabilities are absolutely necessary&lt;/b&gt;

03:33:02.566 --> 03:33:05.569
&lt;b&gt;yes, so that's the core of this paper&lt;/b&gt;

03:33:05.569 --> 03:33:06.636
&lt;b&gt;and this paper&lt;/b&gt;

