&lt;b&gt;and vision has a double meaning&lt;/b&gt;

03:34:53.643 --> 03:34:56.580
&lt;b&gt;it's a very ambiguous word&lt;/b&gt;

03:34:56.580 --> 03:34:57.948
&lt;b&gt;vision refers to both your eyesight&lt;/b&gt;

03:34:58.381 --> 03:35:00.784
&lt;b&gt;and your foresight about the future&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:01.952 --> 03:35:03.887
&lt;b&gt;right, when you say someone has great vision&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:03.887 --> 03:35:04.554
&lt;b&gt;meaning they have a grand vision&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:04.554 --> 03:35:06.623
&lt;b&gt;visionary, vision, yes&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:06.957 --> 03:35:08.758
&lt;b&gt;um, so I think computer vision&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:08.758 --> 03:35:10.627
&lt;b&gt;actually&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:10.627 --> 03:35:12.462
&lt;b&gt;I'm not going to&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:12.629 --> 03:35:14.998
&lt;b&gt;um, this&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:14.998 --> 03:35:16.266
&lt;b&gt;I can say I am someone who&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:16.266 --> 03:35:17.334
&lt;b&gt;works in computer vision&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:17.434 --> 03:35:20.070
&lt;b&gt;yes, but computer vision in my definition&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:20.403 --> 03:35:21.872
&lt;b&gt;it's a perspective&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:22.005 --> 03:35:24.474
&lt;b&gt;it's not a specific task&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:24.608 --> 03:35:25.575
&lt;b&gt;it's not even a&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:25.575 --> 03:35:26.743
&lt;b&gt;specific field&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:27.277 --> 03:35:28.745
&lt;b&gt;it's a perspective&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:28.745 --> 03:35:30.747
&lt;b&gt;perspective means it's a point of view&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:31.548 --> 03:35:33.183
&lt;b&gt;yes, or rather it is&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:33.750 --> 03:35:37.554
&lt;b&gt;I think intelligence — it's quite fundamental&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:37.821 --> 03:35:41.391
&lt;b&gt;it's a collection of problems&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:41.391 --> 03:35:42.959
&lt;b&gt;that intelligence must solve&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:43.593 --> 03:35:44.594
&lt;b&gt;it's a collection&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:45.161 --> 03:35:46.696
&lt;b&gt;right, let me be more specific&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:46.696 --> 03:35:47.797
&lt;b&gt;so what is vision&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:47.797 --> 03:35:49.232
&lt;b&gt;or what problems does vision address&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:49.232 --> 03:35:49.633
&lt;b&gt;mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:49.633 --> 03:35:50.934
&lt;b&gt;I may not be able to articulate it clearly&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:50.934 --> 03:35:51.735
&lt;b&gt;let me think&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:51.801 --> 03:35:52.202
&lt;b&gt;um,&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:52.202 --> 03:35:56.673
&lt;b&gt;first, the signals it handles are in continuous space&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:56.673 --> 03:35:58.808
&lt;b&gt;high-dimensional, noisy signals&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:58.808 --> 03:35:59.576
&lt;b&gt;mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

03:35:59.576 --> 03:36:01.845
&lt;b&gt;right, these are the problems computer vision needs to solve&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:02.412 --> 03:36:03.346
&lt;b&gt;the problems computers need to solve&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:03.346 --> 03:36:05.582
&lt;b&gt;it's not about writing lots of text on paper&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:05.582 --> 03:36:07.817
&lt;b&gt;we need to evolve some kind of intelligence&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:07.817 --> 03:36:08.852
&lt;b&gt;that doesn't avoid this problem&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:09.152 --> 03:36:10.353
&lt;b&gt;it addresses this domain&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:10.353 --> 03:36:11.254
&lt;b&gt;its&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:11.254 --> 03:36:12.155
&lt;b&gt;its target&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:12.155 --> 03:36:13.023
&lt;b&gt;this domain&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:13.056 --> 03:36:14.958
&lt;b&gt;is completely different from language&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:16.359 --> 03:36:17.160
&lt;b&gt;right&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:17.227 --> 03:36:19.963
&lt;b&gt;continuous, high-dimensional, noisy signals&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:19.996 --> 03:36:21.231
&lt;b&gt;these are the problems Vision needs to solve&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:22.332 --> 03:36:25.001
&lt;b&gt;second, from the very first day of doing Vision&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:25.135 --> 03:36:27.671
&lt;b&gt;from the first paper I just mentioned&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:27.671 --> 03:36:31.741
&lt;b&gt;starting from DSN or HED&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:31.741 --> 03:36:32.842
&lt;b&gt;I already knew&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:32.842 --> 03:36:35.078
&lt;b&gt;or rather I had this kind of bet&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:35.078 --> 03:36:35.679
&lt;b&gt;that vision&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:35.679 --> 03:36:37.781
&lt;b&gt;the most important thing&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:37.781 --> 03:36:39.983
&lt;b&gt;is to learn this kind of hierarchical representation&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:39.983 --> 03:36:41.451
&lt;b&gt;hierarchical representation&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:41.885 --> 03:36:43.553
&lt;b&gt;this is extremely important&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:44.254 --> 03:36:46.456
&lt;b&gt;if your representation lacks hierarchy&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:46.590 --> 03:36:49.459
&lt;b&gt;you won't be able to solve&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:49.559 --> 03:36:52.295
&lt;b&gt;many, many problems in this world&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:52.629 --> 03:36:55.966
&lt;b&gt;the hierarchical process is an abstraction process&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:56.199 --> 03:36:57.067
&lt;b&gt;the process of abstraction&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:57.067 --> 03:36:59.369
&lt;b&gt;is what's called a generalization process&lt;/b&gt;

03:36:59.369 --> 03:37:00.737
&lt;b&gt;a generalization process&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:01.471 --> 03:37:04.174
&lt;b&gt;this is also very different from a language model&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:04.174 --> 03:37:05.075
&lt;b&gt;because a language model&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:05.075 --> 03:37:07.077
&lt;b&gt;operates purely in the semantic space&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:07.077 --> 03:37:08.612
&lt;b&gt;when thinking about this problem&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:09.245 --> 03:37:11.348
&lt;b&gt;so&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:11.348 --> 03:37:12.449
&lt;b&gt;there are of course other characteristics&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:12.449 --> 03:37:14.951
&lt;b&gt;for example, I say vision as a perspective, um&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:14.951 --> 03:37:18.021
&lt;b&gt;for example, I think it's also&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:18.021 --> 03:37:19.622
&lt;b&gt;this kind of large-scale parallelization&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:19.622 --> 03:37:21.458
&lt;b&gt;we can now see many, many things&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:21.558 --> 03:37:23.994
&lt;b&gt;many areas of our brain's cortex are firing&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:24.060 --> 03:37:24.628
&lt;b&gt;right, and then&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:24.628 --> 03:37:25.562
&lt;b&gt;we're processing in parallel&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:25.562 --> 03:37:27.097
&lt;b&gt;many many different objects&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:27.097 --> 03:37:28.398
&lt;b&gt;and their&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:28.398 --> 03:37:29.432
&lt;b&gt;causal patterns&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:29.432 --> 03:37:31.868
&lt;b&gt;and their physical changes&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:32.669 --> 03:37:35.638
&lt;b&gt;these things are happening at different times&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:35.638 --> 03:37:37.040
&lt;b&gt;and in different spaces&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:37.040 --> 03:37:38.742
&lt;b&gt;all simultaneously&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:38.742 --> 03:37:40.343
&lt;b&gt;and we have a way&lt;/b&gt;

03:37:40.343 --> 03:37:42.145
