03:43:32.195 --> 03:43:34.797
&lt;b&gt;that we need to deal with the real world&lt;/b&gt;

03:43:34.797 --> 03:43:35.832
&lt;b&gt;real tasks&lt;/b&gt;

03:43:36.466 --> 03:43:38.601
&lt;b&gt;to build some kind of real intelligence&lt;/b&gt;

03:43:38.868 --> 03:43:39.669
&lt;b&gt;ah&lt;/b&gt;

03:43:39.736 --> 03:43:43.139
&lt;b&gt;then this currently imperfect&lt;/b&gt;

03:43:43.139 --> 03:43:44.440
&lt;b&gt;visual representation&lt;/b&gt;

03:43:44.574 --> 03:43:46.743
&lt;b&gt;will be a major deficiency&lt;/b&gt;

03:43:47.877 --> 03:43:49.846
&lt;b&gt;so Yann LeCun's view is&lt;/b&gt;

03:43:50.179 --> 03:43:52.448
&lt;b&gt;everyone right now is just using a crutch&lt;/b&gt;

03:43:52.448 --> 03:43:54.584
&lt;b&gt;that crutch being the language model itself&lt;/b&gt;

03:43:54.817 --> 03:43:56.786
&lt;b&gt;right, and even though you can walk&lt;/b&gt;

03:43:56.786 --> 03:43:57.620
