&lt;b&gt;ratio like C=6ND&lt;/b&gt;

03:50:30.646 --> 03:50:31.614
&lt;b&gt;meaning your&lt;/b&gt;

03:50:31.781 --> 03:50:35.351
&lt;b&gt;your compute is basically equal to 6 times&lt;/b&gt;

03:50:35.418 --> 03:50:37.186
&lt;b&gt;your tokens times your&lt;/b&gt;

03:50:37.186 --> 03:50:39.588
&lt;b&gt;number of parameters&lt;/b&gt;

03:50:40.689 --> 03:50:42.758
&lt;b&gt;and I want&lt;/b&gt;

03:50:42.758 --> 03:50:44.660
&lt;b&gt;I want to use this&lt;/b&gt;

03:50:44.660 --> 03:50:46.762
&lt;b&gt;formal definition to make this point&lt;/b&gt;

03:50:46.762 --> 03:50:47.830
&lt;b&gt;because I now think&lt;/b&gt;

03:50:47.830 --> 03:50:51.400
&lt;b&gt;more and more that vision doesn't need a Scaling Law&lt;/b&gt;

03:50:52.001 --> 03:50:53.135
&lt;b&gt;oh, why is that&lt;/b&gt;

03:50:54.270 --> 03:50:55.237
&lt;b&gt;because again&lt;/b&gt;

03:50:55.237 --> 03:50:57.006
&lt;b&gt;what vision cares about&lt;/b&gt;

03:50:57.807 --> 03:51:00.342
&lt;b&gt;is completely different from what language cares about&lt;/b&gt;

03:51:01.677 --> 03:51:03.612
&lt;b&gt;it's not a radical claim&lt;/b&gt;

03:51:03.612 --> 03:51:04.747
&lt;b&gt;but it is a viewpoint&lt;/b&gt;

03:51:04.747 --> 03:51:05.347
&lt;b&gt;a long-held view&lt;/b&gt;

03:51:05.347 --> 03:51:06.649
&lt;b&gt;and many people doing NLP&lt;/b&gt;

03:51:06.649 --> 03:51:07.983
&lt;b&gt;actually agree with this view&lt;/b&gt;

03:51:08.384 --> 03:51:10.286
&lt;b&gt;that is, a language model&lt;/b&gt;

03:51:10.286 --> 03:51:13.389
&lt;b&gt;is actually not a self-supervised learning process&lt;/b&gt;

03:51:14.156 --> 03:51:15.958
&lt;b&gt;it's actually a strongly&lt;/b&gt;

03:51:15.958 --> 03:51:17.393
&lt;b&gt;supervised learning process&lt;/b&gt;

03:51:18.194 --> 03:51:20.796
&lt;b&gt;meaning it's a strongly supervised process&lt;/b&gt;

03:51:21.730 --> 03:51:22.765
&lt;b&gt;it depends on how you look at it&lt;/b&gt;

03:51:22.765 --> 03:51:24.633
&lt;b&gt;what does supervised or unsupervised mean&lt;/b&gt;

03:51:24.867 --> 03:51:27.036
