04:35:27.707 --> 04:35:29.409
&lt;b&gt;even though it has no actions&lt;/b&gt;

04:35:29.409 --> 04:35:31.578
&lt;b&gt;it has no real understanding of the physical world&lt;/b&gt;

04:35:31.678 --> 04:35:34.280
&lt;b&gt;and it can't truly reason and plan&lt;/b&gt;

04:35:34.280 --> 04:35:36.616
&lt;b&gt;because its planning through CoT&lt;/b&gt;

04:35:36.616 --> 04:35:38.485
&lt;b&gt;and its reasoning through CoT&lt;/b&gt;

04:35:38.485 --> 04:35:39.252
&lt;b&gt;is still very different&lt;/b&gt;

04:35:39.252 --> 04:35:40.053
&lt;b&gt;from what I just described&lt;/b&gt;

04:35:40.053 --> 04:35:41.521
&lt;b&gt;like MPC-level&lt;/b&gt;

04:35:41.521 --> 04:35:43.056
&lt;b&gt;planning&lt;/b&gt;

04:35:43.056 --> 04:35:44.324
&lt;b&gt;CoT also brings its own set of problems&lt;/b&gt;

04:35:44.324 --> 04:35:45.291
&lt;b&gt;but all that's fine&lt;/b&gt;

04:35:45.859 --> 04:35:47.127
&lt;b&gt;but the next step&lt;/b&gt;

04:35:47.127 --> 04:35:47.660
&lt;b&gt;you'll see&lt;/b&gt;

04:35:47.660 --> 04:35:51.731
&lt;b&gt;for example everyone's doing&lt;/b&gt;

04:35:51.931 --> 04:35:52.799
&lt;b&gt;whether DiT or&lt;/b&gt;

04:35:52.799 --> 04:35:54.033
&lt;b&gt;whatever model&lt;/b&gt;

04:35:54.033 --> 04:35:57.270
&lt;b&gt;but people started doing generative models&lt;/b&gt;

04:35:57.270 --> 04:36:00.874
&lt;b&gt;and that has made things somewhat different&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:00.874 --> 04:36:01.241
&lt;b&gt;right?&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:01.241 --> 04:36:02.509
&lt;b&gt;mm-hmm, and that's why many people&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:02.509 --> 04:36:04.444
&lt;b&gt;who do video generation call it a world model&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:04.444 --> 04:36:06.446
&lt;b&gt;I think that's understandable&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:06.446 --> 04:36:06.846
&lt;b&gt;although&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:06.846 --> 04:36:09.716
&lt;b&gt;I don't agree that the video generation&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:09.716 --> 04:36:10.617
&lt;b&gt;model they're doing&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:10.617 --> 04:36:13.686
&lt;b&gt;is the final end game world model&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:13.686 --> 04:36:17.056
&lt;b&gt;but it has indeed pushed one step beyond language models&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:17.724 --> 04:36:19.058
&lt;b&gt;right&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:19.058 --> 04:36:20.460
&lt;b&gt;how does it do that?&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:20.460 --> 04:36:22.829
&lt;b&gt;on top of language models&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:23.129 --> 04:36:23.730
&lt;b&gt;uh&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:23.730 --> 04:36:25.798
&lt;b&gt;I think all these systems now&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:25.798 --> 04:36:28.468
&lt;b&gt;actually still rely on language models&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:28.635 --> 04:36:29.068
&lt;b&gt;right?&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:29.068 --> 04:36:32.238
&lt;b&gt;they still use language models to do prompt&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:32.238 --> 04:36:34.374
&lt;b&gt;rewriting and then to help&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:34.407 --> 04:36:36.242
&lt;b&gt;serve as a conditioning&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:36.442 --> 04:36:38.912
&lt;b&gt;fed into the video generation model&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:38.912 --> 04:36:41.881
&lt;b&gt;and language models have actually become&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:41.881 --> 04:36:43.183
&lt;b&gt;you know&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:43.183 --> 04:36:44.517
&lt;b&gt;the historical progression here is quite interesting&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:44.517 --> 04:36:45.985
&lt;b&gt;language models used to be the main thing&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:46.152 --> 04:36:47.820
&lt;b&gt;now language models have become&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:47.820 --> 04:36:51.090
&lt;b&gt;a preparatory step for video generation models&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:51.090 --> 04:36:52.258
&lt;b&gt;a scaffolding&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:52.659 --> 04:36:54.694
&lt;b&gt;in the old language models&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:54.694 --> 04:36:56.062
&lt;b&gt;what you modeled was P(y)&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:56.062 --> 04:36:59.165
&lt;b&gt;right?&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;b&gt;and that y is still in some semantic space&lt;/b&gt;

04:36:59.165 --> 04:37:00.867
&lt;b&gt;information in some kind of label space&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:00.867 --> 04:37:03.269
&lt;b&gt;mm-hmm, but now with video generation models&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:03.269 --> 04:37:06.206
&lt;b&gt;what you model is the probability P(x|y)&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:06.839 --> 04:37:07.874
&lt;b&gt;what this means is&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:07.974 --> 04:37:10.176
&lt;b&gt;what you're modeling now is already x&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:10.176 --> 04:37:12.045
&lt;b&gt;x is the data itself&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:12.211 --> 04:37:13.513
&lt;b&gt;your y has become&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:13.513 --> 04:37:16.249
&lt;b&gt;a condition — this is already very different&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:16.249 --> 04:37:16.883
&lt;b&gt;okay&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:16.883 --> 04:37:17.684
&lt;b&gt;why is it so different?&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:17.684 --> 04:37:21.187
&lt;b&gt;it's because when you have a low dimensional y&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:21.187 --> 04:37:21.888
&lt;b&gt;space&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:21.888 --> 04:37:22.589
&lt;b&gt;and then you&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:22.589 --> 04:37:26.392
&lt;b&gt;go to model such a distribution&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:26.392 --> 04:37:27.594
&lt;b&gt;your probability density&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:27.594 --> 04:37:29.696
&lt;b&gt;only competes within your y's distribution&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:29.729 --> 04:37:31.531
&lt;b&gt;meaning&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:31.531 --> 04:37:32.899
&lt;b&gt;the likelihood you assign&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:32.899 --> 04:37:34.634
&lt;b&gt;I'm getting a bit too technical here&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:34.634 --> 04:37:35.835
&lt;b&gt;but anyway&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:35.835 --> 04:37:37.470
&lt;b&gt;or let's not talk about language models first&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:37.470 --> 04:37:37.971
&lt;b&gt;let's first talk about&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:37.971 --> 04:37:38.771
&lt;b&gt;say&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:38.805 --> 04:37:41.608
&lt;b&gt;a model that classifies 1000 categories&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:41.608 --> 04:37:41.975
&lt;b&gt;you can think of&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:41.975 --> 04:37:44.177
&lt;b&gt;these few labels as a precursor to language&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:44.310 --> 04:37:47.380
&lt;b&gt;it's also a low-dimensional vocabulary&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:47.380 --> 04:37:48.181
&lt;b&gt;right?&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:48.214 --> 04:37:50.450
&lt;b&gt;and then&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;b&gt;if you're doing a classification problem like this&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:50.650 --> 04:37:53.820
&lt;b&gt;all the decisions you need to make are&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:53.920 --> 04:37:55.822
&lt;b&gt;if this thing is a cat&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:55.822 --> 04:37:57.056
&lt;b&gt;it can't be a dog&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:57.323 --> 04:37:57.890
&lt;b&gt;right?&lt;/b&gt;

04:37:57.890 --> 04:38:00.326
&lt;b&gt;this thing is constrained by my label set&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:00.326 --> 04:38:01.127
&lt;b&gt;mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:01.828 --> 04:38:04.831
&lt;b&gt;but when you start modeling P(x|y)&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:04.831 --> 04:38:06.432
&lt;b&gt;when you're doing a generative model&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:06.499 --> 04:38:10.403
&lt;b&gt;the likelihood you assign in this case says&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:10.403 --> 04:38:12.905
&lt;b&gt;what phenomena actually exist in the world&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:13.039 --> 04:38:15.174
&lt;b&gt;which things are more likely to exist&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:15.808 --> 04:38:17.577
&lt;b&gt;that becomes very very different&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:17.577 --> 04:38:19.779
&lt;b&gt;right? because what you need to learn now&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:19.779 --> 04:38:21.581
&lt;b&gt;the amount of intelligence information&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:21.581 --> 04:38:23.883
&lt;b&gt;is far greater than what you get from modeling P(Y)&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:24.317 --> 04:38:27.320
&lt;b&gt;you need to understand why in this world&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:27.387 --> 04:38:29.455
&lt;b&gt;a four-legged cat&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:29.455 --> 04:38:31.624
&lt;b&gt;is more common than a three-legged cat&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:31.624 --> 04:38:32.725
&lt;b&gt;right?&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:32.859 --> 04:38:34.827
&lt;b&gt;why if I'm generating a video&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:34.994 --> 04:38:37.030
&lt;b&gt;say I have, I don't know&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:37.030 --> 04:38:38.264
&lt;b&gt;a running video&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:38.631 --> 04:38:40.867
&lt;b&gt;why would I have&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:40.867 --> 04:38:43.503
&lt;b&gt;a smooth running state&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:43.503 --> 04:38:46.005
&lt;b&gt;rather than suddenly hallucinating three legs&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:46.005 --> 04:38:46.906
&lt;b&gt;four legs&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:46.973 --> 04:38:48.074
&lt;b&gt;which is more believable&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:48.074 --> 04:38:49.575
&lt;b&gt;more probable, right?&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:49.575 --> 04:38:50.376
&lt;b&gt;in probability space&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:50.376 --> 04:38:51.177
&lt;b&gt;more probable&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:51.244 --> 04:38:53.680
&lt;b&gt;this already carries enormous amounts of information&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:53.680 --> 04:38:55.181
&lt;b&gt;what you need to model&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:55.181 --> 04:38:57.083
&lt;b&gt;far exceeds what you need to capture in language space&lt;/b&gt;

04:38:57.083 --> 04:39:00.420
&lt;b&gt;or in label space&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:00.420 --> 04:39:00.787
&lt;b&gt;right?&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:00.787 --> 04:39:03.189
&lt;b&gt;you already need some understanding of the world&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:03.289 --> 04:39:05.625
&lt;b&gt;so this is already more&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:05.625 --> 04:39:06.926
&lt;b&gt;in line with the Bitter Lesson in my view&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:07.026 --> 04:39:08.328
&lt;b&gt;meaning&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:08.328 --> 04:39:12.498
&lt;b&gt;you've abandoned more of the&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:12.498 --> 04:39:13.599
&lt;b&gt;cognition in language space&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:13.599 --> 04:39:14.434
&lt;b&gt;and its logic&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:14.434 --> 04:39:16.836
&lt;b&gt;and its syntactic structure&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:16.836 --> 04:39:19.105
&lt;b&gt;and started modeling pixels&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:19.238 --> 04:39:20.273
&lt;b&gt;started modeling&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:20.273 --> 04:39:22.842
&lt;b&gt;the pixels themselves&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:22.909 --> 04:39:24.310
&lt;b&gt;but taking it one step further&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:24.477 --> 04:39:26.179
&lt;b&gt;pixels themselves might also be wrong&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:26.612 --> 04:39:29.615
&lt;b&gt;pixels themselves are also not Bitter Lesson enough&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:29.849 --> 04:39:30.650
&lt;b&gt;mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:31.484 --> 04:39:32.318
&lt;b&gt;what are pixels&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:32.318 --> 04:39:34.620
&lt;b&gt;pixels are a human-defined&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:34.787 --> 04:39:37.323
&lt;b&gt;regular grid&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:37.323 --> 04:39:39.692
&lt;b&gt;just a grid of little boxes&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:39.692 --> 04:39:42.261
&lt;b&gt;each little box might have&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:42.261 --> 04:39:43.930
&lt;b&gt;8 bits of information&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:43.930 --> 04:39:46.699
&lt;b&gt;and you might have this kind of lattice&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:46.699 --> 04:39:48.034
&lt;b&gt;like a cell by cell by cell arrangement&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:48.034 --> 04:39:49.001
&lt;b&gt;this is a pixel&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:49.102 --> 04:39:51.771
&lt;b&gt;this is each frame of the image we see&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:52.004 --> 04:39:52.805
&lt;b&gt;right?&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:53.372 --> 04:39:55.074
&lt;b&gt;this is also an interface&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:55.208 --> 04:39:55.975
&lt;b&gt;mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:55.975 --> 04:39:57.477
&lt;b&gt;this is also made for humans to see&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:58.611 --> 04:39:59.412
&lt;b&gt;right?&lt;/b&gt;

04:39:59.979 --> 04:40:01.180
&lt;b&gt;that's why world simulators&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:01.180 --> 04:40:02.648
&lt;b&gt;why do people think Genie&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:02.648 --> 04:40:03.249
&lt;b&gt;is so cool&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:03.249 --> 04:40:05.084
&lt;b&gt;because we create a video&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:05.084 --> 04:40:06.252
&lt;b&gt;we create a game&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:06.419 --> 04:40:07.520
&lt;b&gt;this is for humans to see&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:08.287 --> 04:40:10.089
&lt;b&gt;but taking it one step further&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:10.089 --> 04:40:11.691
&lt;b&gt;the real Bitter Lesson says&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:12.024 --> 04:40:13.192
&lt;b&gt;I don't need to make it for humans to see&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:13.893 --> 04:40:15.294
&lt;b&gt;why do I need to make it for humans?&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:18.064 --> 04:40:18.664
&lt;b&gt;right?&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:18.664 --> 04:40:19.766
&lt;b&gt;who is it for?&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:21.200 --> 04:40:22.568
&lt;b&gt;it's for your system to see&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:22.568 --> 04:40:23.870
&lt;b&gt;it's for your world to see&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:23.870 --> 04:40:24.504
&lt;b&gt;mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:24.504 --> 04:40:26.305
&lt;b&gt;it depends on what you ultimately want&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:26.305 --> 04:40:27.573
&lt;b&gt;it can be for humans to see&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:28.107 --> 04:40:30.810
&lt;b&gt;but being for humans to see&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:31.010 --> 04:40:32.712
&lt;b&gt;is not the core of a World Model&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:33.079 --> 04:40:34.714
&lt;b&gt;it's the interface of the World Model&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:35.448 --> 04:40:36.816
&lt;b&gt;the World Model itself&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:37.049 --> 04:40:39.018
&lt;b&gt;is spontaneously&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:40.853 --> 04:40:42.588
&lt;b&gt;learning better representations&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:43.256 --> 04:40:45.525
&lt;b&gt;making better predictions&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:45.825 --> 04:40:46.325
&lt;b&gt;right?&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:46.325 --> 04:40:48.127
&lt;b&gt;but this thing itself&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:48.127 --> 04:40:50.463
&lt;b&gt;whether or not you want to generate a cool video&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:50.463 --> 04:40:51.531
&lt;b&gt;is actually irrelevant&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:51.831 --> 04:40:53.199
&lt;b&gt;and whether or not you can answer&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:53.199 --> 04:40:55.601
&lt;b&gt;some questions about your input space&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:55.701 --> 04:40:56.903
&lt;b&gt;is also actually irrelevant&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:57.637 --> 04:40:58.237
&lt;b&gt;so again&lt;/b&gt;

04:40:58.237 --> 04:41:00.506
&lt;b&gt;let me repeat what I was just trying to say&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:01.474 --> 04:41:02.275
&lt;b&gt;each of us&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:02.275 --> 04:41:05.511
&lt;b&gt;is moving forward on the road toward world models&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:05.578 --> 04:41:07.480
&lt;b&gt;the world model is a goal&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:07.880 --> 04:41:09.215
&lt;b&gt;not a specific path&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:09.215 --> 04:41:11.384
&lt;b&gt;uh, not a specific algorithm&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:11.384 --> 04:41:12.885
&lt;b&gt;or a specific technical roadmap&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:14.020 --> 04:41:15.087
&lt;b&gt;and someday&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:15.087 --> 04:41:17.523
&lt;b&gt;we will have a better world model&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:17.890 --> 04:41:18.691
&lt;b&gt;mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:18.891 --> 04:41:20.827
&lt;b&gt;language models will, on top of that&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:20.827 --> 04:41:22.428
&lt;b&gt;also get stronger&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:22.428 --> 04:41:24.664
&lt;b&gt;we'll have better multimodal models&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:24.664 --> 04:41:26.833
&lt;b&gt;that can better understand the world&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:27.266 --> 04:41:29.235
&lt;b&gt;and we'll have better video generation models&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:29.402 --> 04:41:30.069
&lt;b&gt;mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:30.069 --> 04:41:32.438
&lt;b&gt;and I think RAE is&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:32.438 --> 04:41:33.906
&lt;b&gt;an early prototype in this process&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:34.240 --> 04:41:35.041
&lt;b&gt;mm-hmm, yeah&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:35.107 --> 04:41:37.410
&lt;b&gt;so now there's also a very hot concept&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:37.410 --> 04:41:40.246
&lt;b&gt;the so-called Unified Model or Omni Model&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:40.780 --> 04:41:43.015
&lt;b&gt;where people try to stack all the data&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:43.015 --> 04:41:44.417
&lt;b&gt;together&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:44.817 --> 04:41:46.786
&lt;b&gt;so that we can have one system&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:46.919 --> 04:41:48.421
&lt;b&gt;that can do both understanding&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:48.521 --> 04:41:49.622
&lt;b&gt;and generation&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:50.289 --> 04:41:51.824
&lt;b&gt;what people also discuss is&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:51.824 --> 04:41:54.193
&lt;b&gt;does understanding help generation&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:54.193 --> 04:41:55.294
&lt;b&gt;or does generation help understanding&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:55.294 --> 04:41:55.895
&lt;b&gt;mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:55.895 --> 04:41:57.663
&lt;b&gt;I think neither really matters&lt;/b&gt;

04:41:57.897 --> 04:42:01.601
&lt;b&gt;understanding and generation are one&lt;/b&gt;

04:42:01.634 --> 04:42:03.302
&lt;b&gt;both need a real World Model&lt;/b&gt;

04:42:03.302 --> 04:42:04.270
&lt;b&gt;as their foundation&lt;/b&gt;

04:42:04.804 --> 04:42:05.471
&lt;b&gt;right&lt;/b&gt;

04:42:05.471 --> 04:42:08.040
&lt;b&gt;once you have that good World Model&lt;/b&gt;

