06:04:06.454 --> 06:04:07.054
&lt;b&gt;to give a simple example&lt;/b&gt;

06:04:07.054 --> 06:04:08.890
&lt;b&gt;recently there was a paper called LeJEPA&lt;/b&gt;

06:04:09.023 --> 06:04:12.293
&lt;b&gt;and with a very rigorous proof they showed&lt;/b&gt;

06:04:12.293 --> 06:04:15.096
&lt;b&gt;if you want a good representation&lt;/b&gt;

06:04:15.096 --> 06:04:18.633
&lt;b&gt;if you want this representation&lt;/b&gt;

06:04:18.966 --> 06:04:20.768
&lt;b&gt;to be agnostic to your downstream task&lt;/b&gt;

06:04:20.768 --> 06:04:23.471
&lt;b&gt;then it must be an isotropic Gaussian distribution&lt;/b&gt;

06:04:23.571 --> 06:04:24.605
&lt;b&gt;this is a bit technical&lt;/b&gt;

06:04:24.605 --> 06:04:25.606
&lt;b&gt;essentially it means&lt;/b&gt;

06:04:25.606 --> 06:04:26.908
&lt;b&gt;it's a characterization&lt;/b&gt;

06:04:26.908 --> 06:04:28.276
&lt;b&gt;of a certain property of representations&lt;/b&gt;

06:04:28.276 --> 06:04:30.211
&lt;b&gt;and I found&lt;/b&gt;

06:04:30.278 --> 06:04:32.046
&lt;b&gt;this actually has merit&lt;/b&gt;

06:04:32.380 --> 06:04:33.681
&lt;b&gt;truly becoming JEPA&lt;/b&gt;

06:04:33.681 --> 06:04:37.018
&lt;b&gt;is because I feel JEPA is not a model&lt;/b&gt;

06:04:37.485 --> 06:04:39.387
&lt;b&gt;JEPA is not a specific algorithm&lt;/b&gt;

06:04:40.254 --> 06:04:43.591
&lt;b&gt;JEPA is a complete cognitive architecture&lt;/b&gt;

