&lt;b&gt;including&lt;/b&gt;

06:11:26.493 --> 06:11:29.663
&lt;b&gt;like whales also have their own language&lt;/b&gt;

06:11:29.797 --> 06:11:31.298
&lt;b&gt;anyway this is all quite fascinating&lt;/b&gt;

06:11:31.298 --> 06:11:32.633
&lt;b&gt;I highly recommend that book&lt;/b&gt;

06:11:32.633 --> 06:11:33.267
&lt;b&gt;[laughter]&lt;/b&gt;

06:11:33.267 --> 06:11:33.868
&lt;b&gt;and there's also&lt;/b&gt;

06:11:33.868 --> 06:11:35.869
&lt;b&gt;I read about some kind of bird (scrub jays)&lt;/b&gt;

06:11:35.869 --> 06:11:37.204
&lt;b&gt;I forgot what they're called&lt;/b&gt;

06:11:37.238 --> 06:11:39.006
&lt;b&gt;apparently they're very good at&lt;/b&gt;

06:11:39.006 --> 06:11:41.408
&lt;b&gt;if one is burying food&lt;/b&gt;

06:11:41.408 --> 06:11:43.811
&lt;b&gt;burying food underground&lt;/b&gt;

06:11:43.844 --> 06:11:44.879
&lt;b&gt;if it notices&lt;/b&gt;

06:11:44.879 --> 06:11:47.181
&lt;b&gt;that one of its peers saw it happen&lt;/b&gt;

06:11:47.514 --> 06:11:48.883
&lt;b&gt;it will first bury it there&lt;/b&gt;

06:11:48.883 --> 06:11:51.418
&lt;b&gt;then wait for the peer to leave, dig it up&lt;/b&gt;

06:11:51.418 --> 06:11:52.987
&lt;b&gt;and rebury it in a different spot&lt;/b&gt;

06:11:54.255 --> 06:11:56.290
&lt;b&gt;I think that's quite interesting&lt;/b&gt;

06:11:56.290 --> 06:11:57.825
&lt;b&gt;and of course we also know&lt;/b&gt;

06:11:57.825 --> 06:11:59.226
&lt;b&gt;dogs have a keen sense of smell&lt;/b&gt;

06:11:59.226 --> 06:12:01.662
&lt;b&gt;and bats navigate by hearing&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:01.829 --> 06:12:05.633
&lt;b&gt;I think the boundaries of intelligence are very broad&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:05.799 --> 06:12:09.036
&lt;b&gt;people now talk about jagged intelligence&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:09.036 --> 06:12:10.471
&lt;b&gt;so your world model&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:10.471 --> 06:12:14.808
&lt;b&gt;which type of biological intelligence will it aim for first?&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:14.908 --> 06:12:16.210
&lt;b&gt;the goal is of course human intelligence&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:16.210 --> 06:12:18.212
&lt;b&gt;human intelligence is certainly&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:18.212 --> 06:12:19.513
&lt;b&gt;still&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:19.513 --> 06:12:21.582
&lt;b&gt;at least in one dimension still the strongest&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:21.582 --> 06:12:21.916
&lt;b&gt;or&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:21.916 --> 06:12:24.852
&lt;b&gt;it's also what can most benefit the world&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:24.852 --> 06:12:25.386
&lt;b&gt;Mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:25.386 --> 06:12:27.721
&lt;b&gt;so we still want to build a world model&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:27.721 --> 06:12:29.890
&lt;b&gt;toward human-like intelligence&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:29.923 --> 06:12:30.457
&lt;b&gt;Mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:30.457 --> 06:12:33.127
&lt;b&gt;but I just want to let go of human arrogance&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:33.394 --> 06:12:35.629
&lt;b&gt;and recently I've been very inspired by this&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:35.629 --> 06:12:37.665
&lt;b&gt;because I watched Rich Sutton&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:37.665 --> 06:12:39.366
&lt;b&gt;in this&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:39.366 --> 06:12:41.035
&lt;b&gt;podcast&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:41.035 --> 06:12:41.835
&lt;b&gt;talk about a theory&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:41.835 --> 06:12:42.670
&lt;b&gt;because before I&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:42.670 --> 06:12:44.605
&lt;b&gt;didn't know how to address this&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:44.872 --> 06:12:46.206
&lt;b&gt;because people say&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:46.307 --> 06:12:47.675
&lt;b&gt;LLMs are amazing, right?&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:47.775 --> 06:12:49.276
&lt;b&gt;LLMs can now write code&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:49.376 --> 06:12:51.879
&lt;b&gt;can win gold at the IMO and IOI&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:52.079 --> 06:12:54.682
&lt;b&gt;can help us go to the moon and Mars&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:54.982 --> 06:12:56.317
&lt;b&gt;these things are incredible&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:57.217 --> 06:12:59.453
&lt;b&gt;and I can't deny these things&lt;/b&gt;

06:12:59.453 --> 06:13:00.688
&lt;b&gt;they really are impressive&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:00.888 --> 06:13:01.689
&lt;b&gt;right?&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:01.689 --> 06:13:04.825
&lt;b&gt;but Rich Sutton's reply&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:04.825 --> 06:13:05.192
&lt;b&gt;I think&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:05.192 --> 06:13:06.994
&lt;b&gt;was very good — he replied&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:07.194 --> 06:13:09.129
&lt;b&gt;you think these things are great and impressive?&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:09.129 --> 06:13:11.265
&lt;b&gt;that they're hard? well, feel free to think that&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:11.265 --> 06:13:12.499
&lt;b&gt;because I don't think so&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:13.000 --> 06:13:16.570
&lt;b&gt;I think building the intelligence of a squirrel&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:17.104 --> 06:13:18.906
&lt;b&gt;is the hard problem&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:19.573 --> 06:13:21.375
&lt;b&gt;once you have a squirrel's intelligence&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:21.775 --> 06:13:24.011
&lt;b&gt;once you can build a squirrel's intelligence&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:24.011 --> 06:13:26.714
&lt;b&gt;and make it survive in the real world&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:26.780 --> 06:13:27.815
&lt;b&gt;with its own goals&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:27.815 --> 06:13:29.016
&lt;b&gt;its own objectives&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:29.016 --> 06:13:31.618
&lt;b&gt;its own intrinsic rewards as you described&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:31.919 --> 06:13:32.920
&lt;b&gt;it knows hunger&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:32.920 --> 06:13:34.221
&lt;b&gt;it has its own emotions&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:35.022 --> 06:13:37.124
&lt;b&gt;and it can engage in social activities&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:37.925 --> 06:13:42.262
&lt;b&gt;after that, writing code, going to Mars, going to the moon&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:42.262 --> 06:13:44.365
&lt;b&gt;those things would be the easy ones&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:45.265 --> 06:13:45.866
&lt;b&gt;Good&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:45.866 --> 06:13:48.168
&lt;b&gt;I'm gradually coming to strongly agree with this view&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:48.435 --> 06:13:50.237
&lt;b&gt;if you set aside human arrogance&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:50.237 --> 06:13:52.706
&lt;b&gt;building a squirrel's intelligence&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:52.706 --> 06:13:54.375
&lt;b&gt;is actually a harder problem&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:54.641 --> 06:13:56.210
&lt;b&gt;but that's not how it looks to humans&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:56.477 --> 06:13:57.578
&lt;b&gt;from a human's&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:57.578 --> 06:13:59.513
&lt;b&gt;perspective&lt;/b&gt;

06:13:59.513 --> 06:14:00.180
&lt;b&gt;it doesn't seem that way&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:00.180 --> 06:14:02.249
&lt;b&gt;but that's entirely due to human arrogance&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:03.083 --> 06:14:05.419
&lt;b&gt;you're also building human-level intelligence&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:05.586 --> 06:14:06.320
&lt;b&gt;ah, yes&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:06.320 --> 06:14:07.021
&lt;b&gt;but what I mean is&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:07.021 --> 06:14:09.723
&lt;b&gt;human intelligence has many, many aspects&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:09.723 --> 06:14:12.793
&lt;b&gt;human intelligence is not just a language model&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:12.793 --> 06:14:14.928
&lt;b&gt;human intelligence encompasses many types of intelligence&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:14.928 --> 06:14:16.663
&lt;b&gt;that cannot be defined&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:16.663 --> 06:14:19.032
&lt;b&gt;by language models or language itself&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:19.600 --> 06:14:22.202
&lt;b&gt;right, I think that's a core insight&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:22.202 --> 06:14:24.671
&lt;b&gt;What is your definition of intelligence?&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:24.671 --> 06:14:27.374
&lt;b&gt;mm-hmm, so as I was just saying&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:27.374 --> 06:14:28.842
&lt;b&gt;Rich Sutton talked about this&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:28.842 --> 06:14:31.045
&lt;b&gt;he feels that squirrel intelligence is the real intelligence&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:31.478 --> 06:14:34.248
&lt;b&gt;I think his framing is a bit different&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:34.782 --> 06:14:37.084
&lt;b&gt;he's not positioning from a human perspective&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:37.117 --> 06:14:39.186
&lt;b&gt;looking at things from an anthropocentric view&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:39.586 --> 06:14:40.521
&lt;b&gt;he's standing at the universe&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:40.521 --> 06:14:42.322
&lt;b&gt;and the creator's perspective&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:43.057 --> 06:14:44.224
&lt;b&gt;from this angle&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:44.391 --> 06:14:45.459
&lt;b&gt;of course&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:45.626 --> 06:14:48.862
&lt;b&gt;being able to recreate a squirrel&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:48.862 --> 06:14:49.630
&lt;b&gt;is greater than your&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:49.630 --> 06:14:53.901
&lt;b&gt;human civilization in these 530 million years&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:53.901 --> 06:14:56.170
&lt;b&gt;the things created in the last 8 seconds&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:56.470 --> 06:14:58.005
&lt;b&gt;by far&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:58.005 --> 06:14:58.639
&lt;b&gt;in this sense&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:58.639 --> 06:14:59.440
&lt;b&gt;I think&lt;/b&gt;

06:14:59.440 --> 06:15:00.307
&lt;b&gt;that's elevated the discussion&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:00.307 --> 06:15:02.676
&lt;b&gt;I think that elevated perspective has merit&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:02.676 --> 06:15:04.178
&lt;b&gt;but defining intelligence&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:04.178 --> 06:15:07.214
&lt;b&gt;I don't want to give it a definition&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:07.214 --> 06:15:09.783
&lt;b&gt;I think different animals have different intelligence&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:09.783 --> 06:15:12.019
&lt;b&gt;and humans have human-level intelligence&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:12.019 --> 06:15:13.020
&lt;b&gt;Mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:13.086 --> 06:15:16.023
&lt;b&gt;and what I want to encourage everyone to do&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:16.390 --> 06:15:18.025
&lt;b&gt;don't only focus on what&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:18.025 --> 06:15:19.893
&lt;b&gt;we as individuals cannot do&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:20.227 --> 06:15:22.496
&lt;b&gt;pay attention to what we're already doing well&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:22.830 --> 06:15:25.199
&lt;b&gt;pay attention to what a 4-year-old child&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:25.199 --> 06:15:27.868
&lt;b&gt;or a child of a few years old does very well&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:28.202 --> 06:15:29.436
&lt;b&gt;those things&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:29.436 --> 06:15:32.072
&lt;b&gt;are actually what our world model&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:32.306 --> 06:15:34.007
&lt;b&gt;next needs to focus on solving&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:34.241 --> 06:15:35.509
&lt;b&gt;mm-hmm, so this is also&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:35.509 --> 06:15:37.444
&lt;b&gt;why Robotics is ultimately&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:37.444 --> 06:15:38.846
&lt;b&gt;a very fitting outlet&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:39.113 --> 06:15:41.982
&lt;b&gt;because before you talk about AGI&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:41.982 --> 06:15:43.984
&lt;b&gt;or super intelligence&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:44.418 --> 06:15:47.254
&lt;b&gt;can we first have a sufficiently reliable&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:47.387 --> 06:15:48.822
&lt;b&gt;and general robot&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:49.189 --> 06:15:51.024
&lt;b&gt;that can function in our home environment&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:51.024 --> 06:15:52.860
&lt;b&gt;and help with household chores&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:52.860 --> 06:15:55.062
&lt;b&gt;right, because a few-year-old child&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:55.062 --> 06:15:57.231
&lt;b&gt;can actually do many, many household chores&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:57.231 --> 06:15:58.999
&lt;b&gt;there's actually a list&lt;/b&gt;

06:15:58.999 --> 06:16:00.267
&lt;b&gt;you can search for it online&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:00.467 --> 06:16:02.236
&lt;b&gt;a 12-year-old child&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:02.236 --> 06:16:03.904
&lt;b&gt;can basically do all the household chores&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:04.638 --> 06:16:07.674
&lt;b&gt;but is there a robot right now&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:07.808 --> 06:16:10.310
&lt;b&gt;that can function like a 12-year-old child&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:10.577 --> 06:16:12.079
&lt;b&gt;and handle these chores?&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:12.079 --> 06:16:12.880
&lt;b&gt;of course not&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:13.180 --> 06:16:14.281
&lt;b&gt;Jie Tan from DeepMind&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:14.281 --> 06:16:14.781
&lt;b&gt;Jie Tan&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:14.781 --> 06:16:18.085
&lt;b&gt;he also says that robotic development is extremely uneven&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:18.085 --> 06:16:18.986
&lt;b&gt;extremely imbalanced&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:18.986 --> 06:16:20.988
&lt;b&gt;its developmental trajectory compared to a child's&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:20.988 --> 06:16:22.022
&lt;b&gt;is different&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:22.022 --> 06:16:23.223
&lt;b&gt;mm-hmm, for example&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:23.223 --> 06:16:26.994
&lt;b&gt;the physical capabilities of robots' limbs have now surpassed&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:26.994 --> 06:16:29.296
&lt;b&gt;they've already surpassed humans&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:29.296 --> 06:16:29.730
&lt;b&gt;Mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:29.730 --> 06:16:32.399
&lt;b&gt;but many other capabilities are still not as good as a child's&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:32.633 --> 06:16:33.100
&lt;b&gt;because of the brain&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:33.100 --> 06:16:34.635
&lt;b&gt;nobody is building the brain&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:34.668 --> 06:16:36.703
&lt;b&gt;nobody is building a robot brain&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:36.703 --> 06:16:39.239
&lt;b&gt;all the robotics startups&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:39.273 --> 06:16:41.408
&lt;b&gt;including the robotics divisions at big companies&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:41.441 --> 06:16:43.043
&lt;b&gt;haven't solved this&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:43.210 --> 06:16:44.511
&lt;b&gt;Doesn't DeepMind count?&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:44.845 --> 06:16:46.647
&lt;b&gt;DeepMind is now entirely based on Gemini&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:46.847 --> 06:16:49.216
&lt;b&gt;so it's also working within the VLA framework&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:49.216 --> 06:16:50.050
&lt;b&gt;Yes&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:50.050 --> 06:16:51.251
&lt;b&gt;everything converges to&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:51.251 --> 06:16:53.787
&lt;b&gt;Gemini&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:53.787 --> 06:16:54.254
&lt;b&gt;Oh&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:54.254 --> 06:16:57.391
&lt;b&gt;but this needs a second half of pre-training&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:57.391 --> 06:16:57.991
&lt;b&gt;Mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

06:16:57.991 --> 06:17:00.494
&lt;b&gt;in Shunyu Yao's classic formulation&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:00.494 --> 06:17:03.230
&lt;b&gt;[laughter] I think there needs to be a second half&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:03.230 --> 06:17:05.065
&lt;b&gt;but I think this is the second half of pre-training&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:05.065 --> 06:17:05.599
&lt;b&gt;Mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:05.599 --> 06:17:07.668
&lt;b&gt;Jim Fan recently also expressed the same view&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:08.368 --> 06:17:10.404
&lt;b&gt;so this pre-training is the world model&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:10.404 --> 06:17:12.806
&lt;b&gt;who will do this pre-training?&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:13.373 --> 06:17:15.242
&lt;b&gt;that's not clear to me&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:15.409 --> 06:17:15.876
&lt;b&gt;if I knew&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:15.876 --> 06:17:17.878
&lt;b&gt;there was another place that could also do this&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:17.878 --> 06:17:19.379
&lt;b&gt;then I might actually reconsider&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:19.379 --> 06:17:21.448
&lt;b&gt;I wouldn't necessarily need to be&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;b&gt;at this startup&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:21.448 --> 06:17:22.382
&lt;b&gt;doing this myself&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:22.516 --> 06:17:23.317
&lt;b&gt;right?&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:24.051 --> 06:17:25.118
&lt;b&gt;robotics startups&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:25.118 --> 06:17:28.121
&lt;b&gt;have no energy to do this&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:28.121 --> 06:17:30.824
&lt;b&gt;they need to put their resources&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:30.824 --> 06:17:32.626
&lt;b&gt;into the so-called hardware&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:32.626 --> 06:17:33.927
&lt;b&gt;scaling law&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:34.227 --> 06:17:34.861
&lt;b&gt;that is&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:34.861 --> 06:17:36.263
&lt;b&gt;you need to buy more robots&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:36.263 --> 06:17:37.464
&lt;b&gt;to deploy these robots&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:37.464 --> 06:17:40.267
&lt;b&gt;or do these things in simulators&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:40.267 --> 06:17:42.402
&lt;b&gt;these imitation learning approaches&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:42.469 --> 06:17:44.304
&lt;b&gt;that can give you a good enough&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:44.304 --> 06:17:47.808
&lt;b&gt;to solve some specific problems&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:47.808 --> 06:17:49.576
&lt;b&gt;in the short term&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:49.576 --> 06:17:51.645
&lt;b&gt;a robotics team that creates value&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:52.045 --> 06:17:53.013
&lt;b&gt;What about PI (Physical Intelligence)?&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:53.480 --> 06:17:55.215
&lt;b&gt;VLA, right?&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:55.215 --> 06:17:56.049
&lt;b&gt;PI is the same&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:56.049 --> 06:17:58.218
&lt;b&gt;PI is already very, very research-oriented&lt;/b&gt;

06:17:58.485 --> 06:18:00.387
&lt;b&gt;and doing very, very well&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:00.387 --> 06:18:01.021
&lt;b&gt;and is inspiring&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:01.021 --> 06:18:02.055
&lt;b&gt;as a company&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:02.389 --> 06:18:05.092
&lt;b&gt;but again, they won't do pre-training&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:05.092 --> 06:18:06.260
&lt;b&gt;they won't do pre-training&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:07.127 --> 06:18:08.095
&lt;b&gt;they'll take&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:08.095 --> 06:18:11.531
&lt;b&gt;language models as their foundation&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:11.598 --> 06:18:12.065
&lt;b&gt;Yeah&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:12.065 --> 06:18:12.799
&lt;b&gt;right?&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:12.799 --> 06:18:15.435
&lt;b&gt;How should we understand your second half of pre-training?&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:15.669 --> 06:18:16.770
&lt;b&gt;what goes in&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:16.770 --> 06:18:17.571
&lt;b&gt;what comes out&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:17.804 --> 06:18:18.205
&lt;b&gt;I don't know&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:18.205 --> 06:18:19.239
&lt;b&gt;at least the first step is&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:19.306 --> 06:18:20.007
&lt;b&gt;in the long run&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:20.007 --> 06:18:21.108
&lt;b&gt;the inputs are all&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:21.108 --> 06:18:22.876
&lt;b&gt;continuous-space signals as I just described&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:23.076 --> 06:18:24.378
&lt;b&gt;high-dimensional&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:24.478 --> 06:18:25.612
&lt;b&gt;potentially noisy signals&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:25.612 --> 06:18:26.246
&lt;b&gt;Mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:26.246 --> 06:18:28.215
&lt;b&gt;at first it might still be video&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:28.215 --> 06:18:30.817
&lt;b&gt;but we might also have multi-modal encoders&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:30.884 --> 06:18:32.919
&lt;b&gt;to handle different&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:32.919 --> 06:18:34.655
&lt;b&gt;signals beyond visual&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:35.522 --> 06:18:37.291
&lt;b&gt;and the outputs&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:37.291 --> 06:18:38.992
&lt;b&gt;that's a research question&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:39.259 --> 06:18:41.628
&lt;b&gt;the self-supervised question is still unknown&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:41.628 --> 06:18:42.329
&lt;b&gt;I&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:42.329 --> 06:18:44.264
&lt;b&gt;not necessarily unknown&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:44.264 --> 06:18:45.899
&lt;b&gt;but&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:45.899 --> 06:18:47.567
&lt;b&gt;it may become clearer later&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:47.834 --> 06:18:48.635
&lt;b&gt;Mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:49.369 --> 06:18:50.771
&lt;b&gt;but&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:50.771 --> 06:18:52.472
&lt;b&gt;I think&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:52.506 --> 06:18:53.774
&lt;b&gt;it's definitely not that simple&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:53.774 --> 06:18:56.643
&lt;b&gt;but I think that's where the excitement lies&lt;/b&gt;

06:18:58.812 --> 06:19:00.013
&lt;b&gt;I also find it quite interesting&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:00.013 --> 06:19:01.248
&lt;b&gt;because the first time we met&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:01.248 --> 06:19:03.617
&lt;b&gt;you said "you are not the chosen one"&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:03.617 --> 06:19:04.918
&lt;b&gt;"you are just the normal one"&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:04.918 --> 06:19:08.188
&lt;b&gt;why do you like saying this?&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:08.188 --> 06:19:10.524
&lt;b&gt;No&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;b&gt;you see, throughout our conversation we discussed my&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:10.524 --> 06:19:12.459
&lt;b&gt;growth story&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:12.459 --> 06:19:14.594
&lt;b&gt;I&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;b&gt;I didn't expect we'd talk about all this&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:14.594 --> 06:19:17.331
&lt;b&gt;but&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:17.331 --> 06:19:19.399
&lt;b&gt;I definitely don't feel like a chosen one&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:19.399 --> 06:19:23.070
&lt;b&gt;[laughter]&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;b&gt;this quote is actually from a team I love&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:23.070 --> 06:19:24.404
&lt;b&gt;Liverpool, right?&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:24.404 --> 06:19:25.572
&lt;b&gt;I'm a KOP (the famous terrace at Anfield and symbol of devoted Liverpool fans)&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:25.672 --> 06:19:28.041
&lt;b&gt;for over 20 years&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:28.041 --> 06:19:29.209
&lt;b&gt;[laughter]&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:29.209 --> 06:19:31.845
&lt;b&gt;I think there's a bit of compatible spirit&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:31.845 --> 06:19:34.114
&lt;b&gt;and my favorite manager&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:34.114 --> 06:19:35.048
&lt;b&gt;Klopp&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:35.215 --> 06:19:36.183
&lt;b&gt;Jürgen Klopp&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:36.450 --> 06:19:37.284
&lt;b&gt;[laughter]&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:37.284 --> 06:19:40.120
&lt;b&gt;he was half-joking when he said to everyone&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:40.187 --> 06:19:41.121
&lt;b&gt;when another manager&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:41.121 --> 06:19:41.621
&lt;b&gt;José Mourinho&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:41.621 --> 06:19:43.690
&lt;b&gt;said "I am the special one"&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:43.690 --> 06:19:44.925
&lt;b&gt;I'm the special one&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:45.492 --> 06:19:47.994
&lt;b&gt;then Klopp said&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:47.994 --> 06:19:49.129
&lt;b&gt;"I'm not the special one"&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:49.129 --> 06:19:50.864
&lt;b&gt;"I'm the normal one"&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:51.064 --> 06:19:54.501
&lt;b&gt;and I think&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:54.501 --> 06:19:56.036
&lt;b&gt;on one hand he himself is very punk&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:56.036 --> 06:19:57.571
&lt;b&gt;he has that rock 'n' roll spirit&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:57.571 --> 06:19:58.772
&lt;b&gt;[laughter]&lt;/b&gt;

06:19:58.772 --> 06:20:00.107
&lt;b&gt;Uh&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:00.107 --> 06:20:02.376
&lt;b&gt;and he often tells everyone&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:02.376 --> 06:20:04.411
&lt;b&gt;that his role in the team&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:04.578 --> 06:20:06.213
&lt;b&gt;is like a battery&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:06.480 --> 06:20:08.415
&lt;b&gt;he hopes through his own passion&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:08.415 --> 06:20:11.318
&lt;b&gt;and his own energy, you know&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:11.318 --> 06:20:13.053
&lt;b&gt;to let others&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:13.053 --> 06:20:14.121
&lt;b&gt;generate electricity for others&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:14.121 --> 06:20:14.988
&lt;b&gt;empower&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:14.988 --> 06:20:16.189
&lt;b&gt;empower others&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:16.189 --> 06:20:17.057
&lt;b&gt;mm-hmm, right&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:17.057 --> 06:20:18.058
&lt;b&gt;I also want to be that kind of person&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:18.058 --> 06:20:20.260
&lt;b&gt;I also want to be for a team&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:20.260 --> 06:20:22.729
&lt;b&gt;whether that team is in academia&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:22.729 --> 06:20:25.565
&lt;b&gt;or in a startup, a battery&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:25.565 --> 06:20:27.234
&lt;b&gt;I think this is actually not easy&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:27.234 --> 06:20:28.301
&lt;b&gt;because sometimes&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:29.069 --> 06:20:30.971
&lt;b&gt;everyone has their moments of discouragement&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:30.971 --> 06:20:31.471
&lt;b&gt;Mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:31.471 --> 06:20:33.273
&lt;b&gt;I also want to&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:33.707 --> 06:20:34.875
&lt;b&gt;so&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:34.875 --> 06:20:35.776
&lt;b&gt;complain more&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:35.776 --> 06:20:37.611
&lt;b&gt;and let out my feelings&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:37.611 --> 06:20:39.179
&lt;b&gt;but I'm gradually coming to feel&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:39.413 --> 06:20:41.815
&lt;b&gt;in academia, like in front of students&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:41.815 --> 06:20:44.885
&lt;b&gt;and in front of the startup team&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:45.085 --> 06:20:48.622
&lt;b&gt;someone needs to play that battery role&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:48.622 --> 06:20:51.525
&lt;b&gt;or I think Yann is a giant battery&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:51.525 --> 06:20:52.526
&lt;b&gt;he inspired me&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:52.526 --> 06:20:54.861
&lt;b&gt;but I hope to pass this electrical charge through me&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:54.861 --> 06:20:55.896
&lt;b&gt;and send it further&lt;/b&gt;

06:20:57.531 --> 06:21:01.768
&lt;b&gt;What was the last time you felt discouraged, and why?&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:02.602 --> 06:21:04.004
&lt;b&gt;I feel discouraged every day&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:04.004 --> 06:21:06.106
&lt;b&gt;I think it's become&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:06.106 --> 06:21:07.841
&lt;b&gt;a kind of researcher's fate&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:07.841 --> 06:21:11.812
&lt;b&gt;I think everyone has this underlying melancholy&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:12.112 --> 06:21:14.414
&lt;b&gt;because the process of research inquiry&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:14.414 --> 06:21:18.885
&lt;b&gt;is like groping around in a dark&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:18.885 --> 06:21:21.221
&lt;b&gt;lightless place&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:21.221 --> 06:21:22.022
&lt;b&gt;Mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:22.222 --> 06:21:23.523
&lt;b&gt;when you can't see any light&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:23.523 --> 06:21:25.992
&lt;b&gt;you always feel lost and discouraged&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:26.493 --> 06:21:28.595
&lt;b&gt;and when people truly feel&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:28.595 --> 06:21:30.664
&lt;b&gt;this kind of joy&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:30.664 --> 06:21:33.366
&lt;b&gt;it's only when you actually get something working&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:33.667 --> 06:21:34.701
&lt;b&gt;but this part of the time&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:34.701 --> 06:21:35.969
&lt;b&gt;is very, very brief&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:36.269 --> 06:21:39.005
&lt;b&gt;maybe only 5% or 10%&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:39.206 --> 06:21:40.774
&lt;b&gt;Kaiming has said something similar&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:41.975 --> 06:21:44.010
&lt;b&gt;so over time&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:44.010 --> 06:21:45.812
&lt;b&gt;right, eventually everyone's&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:45.812 --> 06:21:49.683
&lt;b&gt;mental state can become concerning&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:49.683 --> 06:21:50.517
&lt;b&gt;but I think it's okay&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:50.517 --> 06:21:51.485
&lt;b&gt;I think&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:51.485 --> 06:21:52.452
&lt;b&gt;Uh&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:52.452 --> 06:21:53.620
&lt;b&gt;I think this era now&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:53.620 --> 06:21:56.590
&lt;b&gt;is still not quite the same as before&lt;/b&gt;

06:21:56.590 --> 06:22:00.227
&lt;b&gt;I think now there's more discussion&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:00.227 --> 06:22:02.662
&lt;b&gt;I think&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;b&gt;this is one of the benefits of this AI wave&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:02.662 --> 06:22:03.463
&lt;b&gt;at least&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:03.496 --> 06:22:04.431
&lt;b&gt;people won't feel&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:04.431 --> 06:22:07.300
&lt;b&gt;like they're in a closed space&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:07.501 --> 06:22:08.835
&lt;b&gt;exploring alone&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:08.969 --> 06:22:11.505
&lt;b&gt;at least people can scroll through Xiaohongshu&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:11.505 --> 06:22:12.906
&lt;b&gt;scroll through Weibo, Zhihu&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:12.906 --> 06:22:15.208
&lt;b&gt;and see how everyone is discussing this&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:15.208 --> 06:22:17.110
&lt;b&gt;I think that's sometimes quite stress-relieving&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:17.210 --> 06:22:19.212
&lt;b&gt;but sometimes it also adds pressure&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:19.212 --> 06:22:21.681
&lt;b&gt;when people criticize you, you don't think that anymore&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:22.315 --> 06:22:26.419
&lt;b&gt;Does your company have people with an entrepreneurial personality?&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:26.419 --> 06:22:27.254
&lt;b&gt;entrepreneurial personality&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:27.254 --> 06:22:28.455
&lt;b&gt;generally quite optimistic&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:28.889 --> 06:22:31.458
&lt;b&gt;I think Yann himself is very optimistic&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:31.458 --> 06:22:32.125
&lt;b&gt;very, very optimistic&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:32.125 --> 06:22:33.260
&lt;b&gt;why isn't he a researcher&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:33.260 --> 06:22:34.694
&lt;b&gt;with that melancholy undercurrent?&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:35.662 --> 06:22:36.897
&lt;b&gt;hmm, I don't know&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:36.897 --> 06:22:39.266
&lt;b&gt;because he's been through hardship&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:39.266 --> 06:22:40.467
&lt;b&gt;and then succeeded&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:40.901 --> 06:22:41.701
&lt;b&gt;Oh&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:41.902 --> 06:22:43.603
&lt;b&gt;he lived through the AI winter&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:43.603 --> 06:22:45.372
&lt;b&gt;and then showed everyone&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:45.372 --> 06:22:46.306
&lt;b&gt;he was right&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:46.373 --> 06:22:47.507
&lt;b&gt;and they were wrong&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:47.641 --> 06:22:49.643
&lt;b&gt;if I went through something like that&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:49.643 --> 06:22:51.711
&lt;b&gt;I might not be so melancholy either&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:51.711 --> 06:22:52.979
&lt;b&gt;he's still quite optimistic&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:52.979 --> 06:22:54.047
&lt;b&gt;I think&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:54.080 --> 06:22:55.582
&lt;b&gt;or rather, his past experiences&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:55.582 --> 06:22:57.717
&lt;b&gt;have also given him more confidence&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:57.717 --> 06:22:59.219
&lt;b&gt;and something he often says is&lt;/b&gt;

06:22:59.452 --> 06:23:00.086
&lt;b&gt;this&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:00.086 --> 06:23:03.123
&lt;b&gt;what happened before with deep learning neural networks&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:03.123 --> 06:23:04.057
&lt;b&gt;is exactly the same&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:04.190 --> 06:23:05.025
&lt;b&gt;which thing?&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:05.025 --> 06:23:06.426
&lt;b&gt;it's that now, world models&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:06.426 --> 06:23:09.629
&lt;b&gt;or whatever you call it&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:09.629 --> 06:23:10.130
&lt;b&gt;the current systems&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:10.130 --> 06:23:11.564
&lt;b&gt;building intelligent systems now&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:11.798 --> 06:23:14.234
&lt;b&gt;he says there's always a small group of people&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:14.901 --> 06:23:16.836
&lt;b&gt;who can clearly see&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:17.270 --> 06:23:19.606
&lt;b&gt;the trajectory of the world's development&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:19.606 --> 06:23:20.874
&lt;b&gt;the progress of technology&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:21.875 --> 06:23:24.444
&lt;b&gt;but they're only a small minority&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:25.178 --> 06:23:26.379
&lt;b&gt;most people can't see it&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:26.813 --> 06:23:27.280
&lt;b&gt;right&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:27.280 --> 06:23:29.316
&lt;b&gt;because most people are busy doing other things&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:30.383 --> 06:23:31.484
&lt;b&gt;back then with deep learning&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:31.484 --> 06:23:33.787
&lt;b&gt;people were doing whatever&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:33.787 --> 06:23:35.322
&lt;b&gt;other things&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:35.322 --> 06:23:36.289
&lt;b&gt;traditional machine learning&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:36.289 --> 06:23:37.457
&lt;b&gt;mm-hmm, and now&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:37.457 --> 06:23:38.258
&lt;b&gt;what you're doing is&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:38.258 --> 06:23:38.992
&lt;b&gt;you can, mm-hmm&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:38.992 --> 06:23:40.093
&lt;b&gt;let's not say it — think about it&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:40.427 --> 06:23:42.696
&lt;b&gt;[laughter]&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:42.696 --> 06:23:43.496
&lt;b&gt;and I think&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:43.496 --> 06:23:45.031
&lt;b&gt;he's actually quite optimistic&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:45.031 --> 06:23:46.700
&lt;b&gt;or rather he has&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:46.700 --> 06:23:47.767
&lt;b&gt;enough confidence&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:47.767 --> 06:23:49.502
&lt;b&gt;and says&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:49.636 --> 06:23:52.706
&lt;b&gt;the things I can see are important things&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:52.706 --> 06:23:54.107
&lt;b&gt;the path I can see&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:54.107 --> 06:23:55.442
&lt;b&gt;is a clear path&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:55.976 --> 06:23:58.445
&lt;b&gt;and on this matter&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:58.445 --> 06:23:59.479
&lt;b&gt;I still believe him quite a lot&lt;/b&gt;

06:23:59.512 --> 06:24:00.780
&lt;b&gt;Have you ever doubted him?&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:01.214 --> 06:24:01.615
&lt;b&gt;Uh&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:01.615 --> 06:24:02.315
&lt;b&gt;as I said&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:02.315 --> 06:24:03.183
&lt;b&gt;I questioned JEPA&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:03.183 --> 06:24:04.284
&lt;b&gt;then understood JEPA&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:04.284 --> 06:24:05.085
&lt;b&gt;then became JEPA&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:05.118 --> 06:24:06.486
&lt;b&gt;so of course there was doubt&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:06.586 --> 06:24:08.822
&lt;b&gt;but I feel that trust in a person&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:08.822 --> 06:24:11.625
&lt;b&gt;and trust in a research direction&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:11.625 --> 06:24:14.027
&lt;b&gt;takes time&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:14.227 --> 06:24:16.262
&lt;b&gt;I was just telling students the other day&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:16.696 --> 06:24:18.565
&lt;b&gt;every time Yann gives a talk&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:18.565 --> 06:24:20.367
&lt;b&gt;he gives exactly the same talk&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:20.700 --> 06:24:21.668
&lt;b&gt;his slides&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:21.668 --> 06:24:24.304
&lt;b&gt;are honestly pretty ugly&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:24.304 --> 06:24:25.105
&lt;b&gt;[laughter]&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:25.171 --> 06:24:26.072
&lt;b&gt;[laughter]&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:26.072 --> 06:24:28.308
&lt;b&gt;but they have his personal style&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:28.508 --> 06:24:29.643
&lt;b&gt;style and design&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:29.643 --> 06:24:30.844
&lt;b&gt;is also interesting&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:30.844 --> 06:24:32.912
&lt;b&gt;some things are originally ugly&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:32.912 --> 06:24:34.080
&lt;b&gt;but if you use them enough&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:34.114 --> 06:24:35.849
&lt;b&gt;and time passes&lt;/b&gt;

06:24:35.849 --> 06:24:37.250
&lt;b&gt;they become the new fashion&lt;/b&gt;

